  "term": "randomized-response technique",
  "definition": "The randomized-response technique is a survey method used to gather more dependable information about sensitive topics while helping protect respondents’ privacy. It includes different model variations whose usefulness can vary depending on the situation and how privacy and efficiency are balanced.",
